    Symbol Types

	The Macroassembler recognizes four classes of symbols:

	o numeric symbols
	o instruction symbols
	o macro symbols
	o pseudo-op symbols

      Numeric Symbols

	Numeric symbols have a specific numeric value.  Because of this
	value, numeric symbols can be used in arithmetic expressions.  A
	label is an example of a numeric symbol.  The numeric value of a
	label is the address with which it is associated.






































