	.PART (continued)

		If a partition is given different attributes in two .PART
		statements, MASM and LINK attempt to resolve the attributes
		and report an error if they cannot be resolved.  The attributes
		are resolved as follows:

			NREL or ZREL		Resolved in favor of ZREL
			LONG or SHORT		Resolved in favor of SHORT
			UNSHARED or SHARED	An error is reported
			CODE or DATA		An error is reported
			NORM or COMM		An error is reported
			GLOBAL or LOCAL		An error is reported
			MESS or NOMESS		Resolved in favor of NOMESS
			Align differences	Resolved in favor of the
						higher alignment
	|		NOENTS or ENTS		Resolved in favor of ENTS


		Example

			.PART   TJ   ALIGN=1,SHORT
			.
			.			  ; This is code in partition TJ
			.ZREL
			.
			.                         ; This is code in ZREL
			.PART   TJ   ALIGN=1,SHORT
			.
			.                         ; This is also code in
			.                         ; partition TJ






















