	Table 8-1  MASM Function Switches
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	  Function Switch	Action
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------

	  /16			Create a 16-bit object file that can be linked
				into a 16-bit process.  By default, AOS/VS MASM
				generates a 32-bit object.  This switch changes
				the structure of the object file and sets the
				default data size size to 1 word, the same as
				.ENABLE WORD pseudo-op.

	  /$			Treat $ as a special character.  By default,
				$ is treated like an alphabetic character.
				Setting this switch causes $ to be expanded
				instead to a number unique to each macro call.

	  /CPL=<n>		Set the number of characters per line on the
				listing and error file.  <n> may be between
				80 and 136, inclusive.  The default number of
				characters per line is 80.

	  /E[=<filename>]	Append the error listing to <filename>.  If
				this switch is omitted, errors are appended to
				@OUTPUT.  If the argument to this is omitted,
				and there is a listing file, the error file
				is suppressed.

	  /ERRORCOUNT=<n>	Terminate MASM with a fatal error if more than
				<n> errors occur.  The default is 1024
				(decimal).

	  /FF			If necessary to produce an even number of
				listing pages, append an extra form feed to
				the listing.

	  /HASH=<n>		Set the hash frame size of the symbol table.
				Set this switch only if /MAKEIN is also set.

	  /L[=<filename>]	Append a MASM listing to <filename>, or to
				@LIST, if <filename> is absent.

	  /LOCAL		Include local (nonglobal) user-defined symbols
				in the object file, as well as global symbols.
				When the /LOCAL switch is also used on Link,
				the local symbols can be used in debugging.

